Date: Wed, 30 Nov 2022 18:46:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] winex11: Use scancode high bit to set
 KEYEVENTF_EXTENDEDKEY flag.

Wine-Bug: https://bugs.winehq.org/show_bug.cgi?id=30984
Wine-Bug: https://bugs.winehq.org/show_bug.cgi?id=45605

Upstreamed in wine-mirror 11.20: X11DRV_KeyEvent keeps the full scan value
(WORD scan), traces it with %04x, and derives KEYEVENTF_EXTENDEDKEY from it
via the scan_is_extended() helper. Only a note remains so the series step
still validates.
---
 dlls/winex11.drv/keyboard.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/dlls/winex11.drv/keyboard.c b/dlls/winex11.drv/keyboard.c
--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/keyboard.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/keyboard.c
@@ -1603,5 +1603,6 @@ BOOL X11DRV_KeyEvent( HWND hwnd, XEvent *xev )
     update_lock_state( hwnd, vkey, event->state, event_time );

     X11DRV_send_keyboard_input( hwnd, vkey & 0xff, scan & 0xff, dwFlags, event_time );
+    /* GE-Proton scancodes 7/9: upstreamed (full scan value, scan_is_extended). */
     return TRUE;
 }
